; descend_to_check FAILURE followed by a SIBLING that must still match, on the
; guaranteed-coref single-source path. For first-arg `aa`/`cc` the size byte 0xC2
; EXISTS at arg 2 but the payload differs -> check fails; the cursor must be restored
; to EXACTLY the pre-symbol position or the later `bb`/`dd` siblings are lost.
; upstream: ascend(size+1) after a check that left the full descent;
; ours: ascend(1) after a check that restored itself. Net position must agree.
(d aa ab)
(d bb bb)
(d cc cd)
(d dd dd)
(exec 0 (, (d $x $x)) (, (out $x)))
